  "description": "PRE-SALES GOING ON NOW!!\n\nA Vision Realized\n\nThis frame represents one of the final designs conceived by Lynskey founder David Lynskey. After decades of designing titanium bicycles, David set out to create the ultimate do-it-all gravel bike—a true Swiss Army knife that could adapt to the rider instead of asking the rider to adapt to the bike.\n\nHis vision was simple: one titanium frame equally at home on pavement, gravel, loaded touring, and everything in between. With the proper slider dropout it is capable of utilizing modern UDH drivetrains, SRAM Transmission, traditional geared builds, or a minimalist single-speed, it was designed to evolve alongside its owner for years of adventure.\n\nToday, that vision lives on in a frame built with the timeless craftsmanship, versatility, and ride quality that defined David's work, while its name takes cues from David's favorite car, the legendary 280Z.\n\nAll complete bikes come with our Industrial Mill frame finish.\n\nComfort for Every Mile\n\nSport Gravel geometry combines a taller stack, shorter reach, and compliant curved seatstays to deliver a confident riding position and exceptional comfort over long days in the saddle.\n\nAdaptable by Design\n\nSliding dropouts support UDH-compatible drivetrains—including SRAM Transmission—or dedicated single-speed sliders, allowing the bike to evolve with your riding.\n\nAdventure Ready\n\nFour bottle mounts, rack and fender mounts, external cable routing, and clearance for up to 700x50c or 650b x 2.1\" tires make this frame equally suited to commuting, bikepacking, and backcountry exploration.\n\nHandcrafted in Chattanooga\n\nBuilt from premium aerospace-grade titanium in Chattanooga, Tennessee, every frame is corrosion resistant, exceptionally durable, and backed by a lifetime warranty.\n\nWhether you're lining up for a gravel race, embarking on a cross-country tour, or simply choosing the long way home, this is the titanium gravel bike built to do it all.",
